{"name":"Blue Smoke","hex":"#d7e0e2","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"smoke","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The visible vapor/vapour, gases, and fine particles given off by burning or smoldering material.","A cigarette."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To inhale and exhale the smoke from a burning cigarette or cigar, burning material in a pipe, etc.","To inhale and exhale tobacco smoke."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smoke"}],"entries":[{"title":"Magic smoke","blocks":[{"text":"Magic smoke is a humorous name for the caustic smoke produced by severe electrical over-stress of electronic circuits or components, causing overheating and an accompanying release of smoke. The smoke typically smells of burning plastic and other chemicals. The color of the smoke depends on which component is overheating, but it is commonly blue, grey, or white. Minor overstress eventually results in component failure, but without pyrotechnic display or release of smoke. A power transistor inside a power supply is a frequent culprit for the acrid smoke."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Magic_smoke.jpg/330px-Magic_smoke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magic_smoke","wikidata":"Q1884089"},{"title":"Aerogel","blocks":[{"text":"Aerogels are a class of synthetic porous ultralight material derived from a gel, in which the liquid component for the gel has been replaced with a gas, without significant collapse of the gel structure. The result is a solid with extremely low density and extremely low thermal conductivity. Aerogels can be made from a variety of chemical compounds. Silica aerogels feel like fragile styrofoam to the touch, while some polymer-based aerogels feel like rigid foams."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Aerogel_hand.jpg/330px-Aerogel_hand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aerogel","wikidata":"Q381490"},{"title":"Blue Smoke (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Smoke is the forty-fourth solo studio album by American country entertainer Dolly Parton. The album was released in Australia and New Zealand on January 31, 2014, in North America on May 13, 2014, in Ireland on June 6, 2014, and in Europe on June 9, 2014."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/15/BlueSmoke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Smoke_(album)","wikidata":"Q15634308"},{"title":"Smoke","blocks":[{"text":"Smoke is an aerosol emitted when a material undergoes combustion or pyrolysis, together with the quantity of air that is entrained or otherwise mixed into the mass. It is commonly an unwanted by-product of fires, but may also be used for pest control (fumigation), communication, defensive and offensive capabilities in the military, cooking, or smoking. It is used in rituals where incense, sage, or resin is burned to produce a smell for spiritual or magical purposes. It can also be a flavoring agent and preservative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg/330px-Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke","wikidata":"Q130768"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Magic_smoke_refill_%285990429717%29_%282%29.jpg/500px-Magic_smoke_refill_%285990429717%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Magic_smoke_refill_%285990429717%29_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Magic_smoke_refill_%285990429717%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Magic_smoke_refill_%285990429717%29_%282%29.jpg/500px-Magic_smoke_refill_%285990429717%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gag IBM magic smoke refill. Note the \"magic smoke\" valve in the instructions.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMagic_smoke_refill_(5990429717)_(2).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/No_blue_smoke.jpg/500px-No_blue_smoke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/No_blue_smoke.jpg/500px-No_blue_smoke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An integrated circuit rendered useless after overheating, the presumptive magic smoke having burnt through","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANo_blue_smoke.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Aerogel_crystals_M25W_%2B2mm_produced_in_ScCO2_drying.jpg/500px-Aerogel_crystals_M25W_%2B2mm_produced_in_ScCO2_drying.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Aerogel_crystals_M25W_%2B2mm_produced_in_ScCO2_drying.jpg/1280px-Aerogel_crystals_M25W_%2B2mm_produced_in_ScCO2_drying.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Aerogel_crystals_M25W_%2B2mm_produced_in_ScCO2_drying.jpg/50